{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested for hosted MCP Draft3 at exact d83243638c31a748e8cabe6df0420945d4d2d5cb, primary13ebdff8d55ab40cef1fe08868563f601f31531f FIRST, normally assigned original f88c4944/705999cf. Design only; no implementation failure or deployed exploit is claimed. Draft3 materially repairs the previous durable creation handoff, byte-partitioned segments, listed/notified state, legacy version validation and error/header precision. Two P2 corrections remain.\n\nP2 1 — Renew and account completion capacity before every dispatch (§3.6,H6). Initial identity admission reserves2MiB record+1MiB segments, then terminal/archive releases it. Native custody299–322 reuses an archived refused identity through #kept and deliberately sends it again without initial admission/build; subsequent step376–408 likewise writes and dispatches a retained identity. After other work fills the budget, that resumed operation may have no remaining completion reservation. Repeated uncertainty/refusal also adds retained outcomes beyond a fixed lifetime allocation. Byte-bounded rows do not bound aggregate history.\n\nSpecify atomic reservation rearm/top-up before send, refused resubmit and repeat step. Count existing serialized record/chunk/segment/index bytes as used; reserve only additional outstanding completion capacity; transfer consumed reservation into used monotonically without double counting or creating free space. If top-up cannot succeed, refuse full before dispatch, retaining every original/outcome and any outstanding reservation still needed by settle. Terminal answer replay must remain readable without requiring a new dispatch reservation. Bound newly growing step state too. H6 needs archived refusal→budget full→explicit resubmit, and repeated uncertain attempts consuming reservations, with reset/readback and unchanged envelope/decisive result.\n\nThe same capacity rule applies to control handoff: reserve complete-answer/tombstone space in both registry and agent budgets before allocation/enrollment. The separate16MiB agent budget does not define registry reservations/list/answers/tombstones. Do not enroll a key and only then discover there is no space to publish create's answer. Keep unfinished reservations resumable; refuse new controls before effectful handoff. A within-budget SQLITE_FULL rollback/readability is not immediate successful settlement while writes keep failing: retain exact unknown custody as a recoverable storage failure and witness receipt recovery once writing succeeds, or specify physically secured completion storage.\n\nP2 2 — Do not claim March2025 is a November alias (§3.4,H8). The draft newly accepts2025-03-26 and2025-06-18 as the same handling, yet rejects every batch. March's transport permits batched POST requests/notifications/responses, so a valid claimed-March request would be rejected as invalid. Keep the originally commissioned2025-11-25 and2026-07-28 support; removing these uncommissioned aliases is not a reduction of that scope. If older revisions are deliberately adopted, provide their distinct behavior map and owning witnesses rather than aliases. Missing-header selection should use known session context or InitializeRequest.protocolVersion when supplied; fallback does not establish support for a different revision. Official primary March source: https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/modelcontextprotocol/blob/main/docs/specification/2025-03-26/basic/transports.mdx\n\nCredit the repaired control design: durable fingerprint→original agent ID before handoff, seed/envelope persistence, bearer/answer before reply, atomic rotation and current-authority replay checks, with H1 resets/concurrent duplicates. Clarify that current-authority validation precedes effectful reservation; seed-only recovery constructs its first envelope, never replaces an already-kept one; freshly signed same-op control renewal is separate from fixed answer-retention and unchanged native-envelope expiry. These are nonblocking implementation precision points.\n\nCredit the bounded Wire change: durable listed written only from tools/list, ephemeral notified per stream, fresh-generation reconnect and replacement-GET ownership, with H5's no-list/reset/reconnect/list cases. Preserve list-state persistence before response emission. Legacy invalid/unsupported headers now refuse before dispatch; id:null, raw header safety, Unicode/whitespace sentinel tests and graceful versus abrupt stream endings are coherent. Add mixed-era header/metadata negatives and response MIME/empty202 assertions to H8.\n\nP3 fidelity: §2 still falsely says membership sees only the secret digest and describes old told only as last-listed; H1's no-hosted-row wording must exempt the retained custody envelope. §3.3/3.5 now correctly explain native plaintext signed history and old Wire notification updates. Align the overview with those accurate sections; do not redact native bytes or weaken custody.\n\nArchitecture: partitioned registry/agent state and one shared service remain suitable; admission accounting must cover the entire recovery lifecycle. Security: signed current authority, native enrollment and preserved originals are retained. Simplification: separate durable logical state from delivery bookkeeping and support explicit revisions; no stateless fallback or arbitrary feature cut.\n\nCoverage: Root FIRST direct FULL40794B631LF SHA5beef979019ca7851cd65a78afe56cd4d729b4da5701004f4a4874027e2f68af in ten bounded contiguous spans/EOF; three peer final reports FULL. Framework U324860B FULL; native support inherited only through actual OWN prior coverage and exact native equality, not whole-module FULL inference. Root independently read current #kept/send/step closures and the official March batch section; web authority is selected excerpts, not whole-page FULL. No runtime/tests/gate/install/provider/browser/private evidence or Source/index edits. H1–H8, one gate, exact implementation review/landing and the recorded live hosted check remain prospective. Discovery remains predecessor; full Stage2, OAuth, reads/resources/prompts, export and Start-link parity remain owed, with no silent expansion/closure of parent34c4.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13ebdff8d55ab40cef1fe08868563f601f31531f","binding":"assigned","head":"d83243638c31a748e8cabe6df0420945d4d2d5cb","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0dc23ebf6713f5e043f7ce159d641b0297529695\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:705999cfd6bcb95dfac0f52bd180fd0df3511439\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0c203045fdd38ac95bc526e546c721fe35b516a5","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}